The full-text record confirms the core result: cross-generation validation from G0/G1 training to G2 yielded accuracies of 0.70–0.85 across circumference, height, and stem straightness. Within-generation accuracy was sensitive to relatedness; including parents nearly eliminated the gap between low- and high-relatedness scenarios. I’ll save these findings and citation in the evidence graph, then answer.

